From 3b04c23d1242a54345fc6bafbd31d41312823513 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sanjitdev <sanjit.majumdar@brainstation-23.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 20:40:31 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] fix(api): ignore pnpm scripts during Docker build +
 rebuild bcrypt
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The root `package.json` `prepare: husky` script fires during
`pnpm install` and the husky binary isn't in the filtered deps
for the api image. The script therefore crashed the Docker build
with `husky: not found` (the install step returned non-zero
before pnpm could link binaries).

Two fixes:

1. Pass `--ignore-scripts` to both `pnpm install` invocations
   (deps stage line 33, runtime stage line 95). This dodges the
   husky `prepare` hook entirely — the runtime image doesn't
   need git hooks.

2. Add `pnpm rebuild --filter @surakkha/api... bcrypt` after
   each install. The `--ignore-scripts` flag suppresses the
   bcrypt postinstall (native binding compile), so without an
   explicit rebuild the api boots with
   `Could not locate the bindings file ... .node` and crashes
   on the first `bcrypt.hash` call. The rebuild recompiles
   bcrypt against the Debian-slim runtime ABI.

Co-Authored-By: Opus 4.8 <noreply@puku.sh>
