MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three MJS seed scripts under `packages/db/` exist as
workarounds for the (currently broken) `pnpm seed` command:

- `seed-devices.mjs` — upserts the 6 demo devices so the
  simulator's telemetry ingest doesn't FK-violate on
  `Reading.deviceId`.
- `seed-rules.mjs` — inserts the FR-13 default rule set
  (9 rules across pH, TDS, turbidity, chlorine, temp,
  water_level). Defaults to `minDurationSeconds=0` +
  `hysteresisSeconds=0` which trips the Story 3.4 boot
  guard — apply the SQL one-liner from RUNBOOK.md §4b
  after seeding (`UPDATE "Rule" SET "hysteresisSeconds"
  = 10 WHERE "isActive" = true;`).
- `seed-incidents.mjs` — creates 5 incidents spanning
  every Kanban column state (OPEN, ACKNOWLEDGED,
  INSPECTING, MONITORING, SAFE) with a matching
  IncidentEvent timeline. Bypasses the rule engine
  because the cached api image may predate Story 3.4's
  de-bouncing wiring; gives the Kanban + Incident
  Detail Page (Story 4.4) populated data for visual
  verification.

Each script starts with `/* eslint-env node */` — the
root `eslint.config.js` declares the Node + browser globals
only for `*.ts`/`*.tsx` globs; `.mjs` files fall through
to `js.configs.recommended` and need the explicit env
directive to keep `console` / `process` from triggering
`no-undef` in the lint-staged pre-commit hook. The
incidents script also drops an unused `ADMIN_ID`
constant the linter was flagging.

Also ship `docker-compose.local.yml` — the day-to-day
run layer that uses the cached `surakkha-dev-{api,web,
simulator}:latest` images built by `docker-compose.dev.yml`.

The `RUNBOOK.md` (separate file in this same commit) is
the canonical entry point for these scripts and walks a
fresh agent through the boot order, seed workflow,
smoke testing, and the five operational pitfalls (the
catch-all 404 order, the `/auth/login` path, the
"healthy" container with a dead api, the `--ignore-scripts`
+ bcrypt dance, and the cached image that isn't recreated
automatically).

`AGENTS.md` §7 gets a step-3 entry pointing at
RUNBOOK.md so the next agent that hears "run the
project" knows where to look without having to rediscover
the boot sequence.

`.gitignore` also gets `tmp/` and `.review-target-*.txt` so
one-off agent probes and BMAD placeholder files don't
pollute `git status`.

