From 8e8be1db62e50bd021b0dbcf0736d2c0ceb93319 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sanjitdev <sanjit.majumdar@brainstation-23.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 12:33:47 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] =?UTF-8?q?chore(4.4):=20review-iteration=20patches=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20typed=20the=20read-side=20detail=20surface?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Step-04 review of `spec-4-4-incident-detail-page.md` surfaced
~30 adversarial findings + ~25 edge-case paths + 7 verification
gaps. Triage routes most of these to `defer` (forward-compat
enum drift, intra-mount id transitions, internationalization,
etc.) or `reject` (noise). The patches below are the
"caused-or-exposed-by-this-change" fixes the review surfaced:

**Code**

- `IncidentDetailPage.tsx` — collapse the duplicate
  `IncidentDetailEnvelope` / `IncidentDetailRow` interfaces into
  one (`IncidentDetailEnvelope` was the actual envelope, the
  Row alias was unused ceremony). Drop `[...queryKey]` spread
  on the row query + invalidate call — `incidentDetailQueryKey`
  already returns a readonly tuple; the spread was dead work.

- `useIncidentDetailSocket.ts` — rename `KANBAN_SOCKET_URL` →
  `DEFAULT_SOCKET_URL`. The constant is the shared dashboard
  socket URL, not a Kanban-domain concern; the old name leaked
  the Kanban naming from the detail file.

- `NotFound.tsx` — drop dead `not-found-back` CSS class. The
  style is set inline (PRIMARY bg); no stylesheet rule references
  this class.

- `router.ts` — strip raw incident UUID from the
  `console.error` log line on the timeline endpoint. UUIDs in
  log lines are PII-adjacent (they identify the affected
  resource) and add nothing diagnostic — the response shape
  is already `{ error: "internal_error" }`.

**Tests**

- `cacheMutators.spec.ts` — replace the single
  `does NOT special-case RESOLVED` case with a parametrized
  `describe.each` over `INCIDENT_STABLE_STATES`. The no-special-case
  contract is now structurally pinned — any future contributor
  who adds per-state logic to the shared helper breaks the
  table.

- `IncidentDetailPage.spec.tsx` — rename the timeline-404
  test from "renders <NotFound /> when the row succeeds but the
  timeline returns 404" to "renders the row + empty timeline
  (NOT <NotFound />) when the timeline returns 404" + add an
  `expect(screen.queryByTestId("not-found")).toBeNull()` pin.
  The old name lied about the contract; the actual implementation
  only renders NotFound on a row-level 404.

- `NotFound.spec.tsx` — NEW dedicated unit test. Covers the
  default render (role=status, aria-live=polite, default
  headline + message + backHref=/incidents + backLabel), the
  override-prop surface (headline / message / backHref /
  backLabel), and the back link's `href` target. The first
  404 surface in the codebase now has its own contract pin —
  future per-entity detail pages (4.5 / 4.6 / 4.7 / 4.11) reuse
  this with confidence.

**Verification**

- `pnpm -r typecheck` — clean.
- `pnpm -F @surakkha/api test` — 401 pass / 5 fail. The 5
  failures are pre-existing in `alerts/listRouter.spec.ts`
  (Story 3.5 test-fixture drift; tracked as AI-3.1 in the
  retrospective, NOT this story's surface). All
  `incidents/router.spec.ts` (45 tests) including the new
  timeline endpoint tests pass.
- `pnpm -F @surakkha/web test` — 297 / 297 pass. Includes the
  new `cacheMutators` parametrized table (11 tests, was 5)
  and the new `NotFound.spec.tsx` (4 tests).

